Douglas Berry wrote:
> I recently have started playing a lot of monks for some reason, and
> since these tend to be quick deaths for me, I was wondering if anyone
> had advice about playing them?

I always play mine vegetarian weaponless body armorless.

> Best alignment choice?

If you don't go artifact wishless, neutral.  Monks at high levels are
spell-casters, and the Eye is incredible.  Also gives MR, so they can
keep the robe on.  Without an MR-granting artifact (remember that your
own quest artifact can be stolen, and the most likely thief has the
touch of death!), you pretty much need to wear CoMR unless you're going
to wear body armor (possible at high levels, but out of character IMO).
 Chaotic is worst since they don't have any artifact wishes that give
MR without severe restriction (I think they can wish for magicbane but
that needs to be wielded, making weaponless tough, and wielded weapons
are thievery targets).  I like the Mirror for lawfuls, since ESP is
handy for vegetarians and it gives MR.

> What are good wishes?

If you're artifact wishless, speed boots, CoMR, or shield/amulet of
reflection depending on situation (blessed greased fixed +3 for all).
Be aware that the shield penalizes spellcasting (my ascension went with
amulet, but from Soko not wish).  Basically the same idea as other
classes, but your MR/reflection sources don't include DSM so you look
to alternative sources.

> Should I get GoPower and kick ass, or G-Dex and stock up on magic?

Dex, definitely.  18/** strength gives most (all?) of the benefits of
GoP without interfering with magic, and monks are good spellcasters.



